---
import AdSlot from "../components/AdSlot.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Corrections & Clarifications — PULSE"
  description="How to report an error in a PULSE story, and how we handle corrections once confirmed."
>
  <div class="container-page-wide flex justify-center pt-4 pb-2">
    <AdSlot slot="leaderboard-top" format="leaderboard" label="Advertisement" />
  </div>

  <section class="container-page max-w-[720px] pt-10 pb-14">
    <span class="eyebrow eyebrow-accent">About PULSE</span>
    <h1 class="section-title mt-2 text-[clamp(28px,4.5vw,40px)]">Corrections & clarifications</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink-3">
      We correct factual errors as soon as we confirm them. This page explains how that works and how to
      flag something that looks wrong.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-9">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl">How to report an error</h2>
        <p class="mt-2.5 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink-3">
          Email <a href="mailto:corrections@pulse.example" class="font-bold text-primary hover:underline">corrections@pulse.example</a>
          with the article headline or link and a description of what's wrong. Include a source for the
          correct information if you have one — it speeds up verification. See our full
          <a href="/contact" class="font-bold text-primary hover:underline">contact page</a> for other ways
          to reach us.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl">What happens next</h2>
        <p class="mt-2.5 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink-3">
          An editor — not the original reporter alone — verifies the claim. If confirmed, we fix the
          article and add a short correction note stating what changed and when. For errors serious enough
          to affect the story's central point, we also note it prominently at the top of the piece rather
          than only at the bottom.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl">Clarifications vs. corrections</h2>
        <p class="mt-2.5 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink-3">
          A <strong class="text-ink">correction</strong> fixes a factual error. A
          <strong class="text-ink">clarification</strong> adds context or rewords something ambiguous
          without the original having been factually wrong. We label each one accordingly rather than
          bundling them together.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 rounded-lg border border-border bg-bg-soft p-6">
      <h3 class="text-sm font-extrabold tracking-[0.04em] text-ink-3 uppercase">Recent corrections</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-4">
        No corrections have been issued recently. When one is, it'll be listed here alongside a link to
        the affected story.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
